<<
/Title (Our focus on minority issues this year aims to foster greater empathy and awareness for marginalized communities across the globe. So that delegates can acknowledge their own privilege and responsibility for standing up for others, ensuring that they will contribute to upholding the moral fabric of equality in society.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 25 0 R
/Prev 823 0 R
/Next 731 0 R
>>
endobj
825 0 obj
<<
/Title (BDCMUN is committed to providing a platform for youthful minds to tackle issues of global significance, fostering a diplomatic attitude amongst delegates in the process and offering a chance to explore the multi-dimensional avenues of public speaking. This includes everything from informal debate in Unmoderated Caucuses to the formal debate in the General Speakers List. We aim to promote discourse in all its forms.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 328 0 R
/Prev 732 0 R
/Next 826 0 R
>>
endobj
826 0 obj
<<
/Title (Our well-equipped, competent host team is ensuring an engaging and exciting experience for all of you, while creating a friendly environment that cultivates a deeper understanding of the United Nations proceedings and peacekeeping mechanisms. We are confident in the ability of Lahore's MUN circuit and our host team that this conference will be one where the principles of diplomacy, as manifested by high schoolers, live on in every setting.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 328 0 R
/Prev 825 0 R
/Next 733 0 R
>>
endobj
827 0 obj
<<
/Title (It is my honour to invite you to the second edition of the BDC MUN conference. I've been coaching BDC for the past three years and have developed a great love and deep passion for the society. We have a very principled society with dynamic sessions, structured debates, and a strong emphasis on the art of debates, public speaking, and diplomacy.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 571 0 R
/Prev 734 0 R
/Next 933 0 R
>>
endobj
